Subject: [PATCH 1/2] provider: a Google account's quota names the plan Code
 Assist reports now (#5621, 0xTotoroX)

The account's saved plan from sign-in (Antigravity Starter Quota) kept
overwriting what Code Assist's project data reports (Google AI Pro):
googleAccount.quota took the project's plan only when the quota had none
to begin with, so the stale saved name never updated. The project's
non-empty plan (paid tier first) is now the one shown; the saved plan is
only a fallback for a reading that can't name one. The reported face is
a Pro upgrade showing the old Starter label; a downgrade now shows too.

Patch by 0xTotoroX (issue #5621), applied as posted; regression tests
theirs (TestGoogleQuotaPlanFollowsCodeAssist new,
TestAntigravityTierAskedAgainAfterUpgrade strengthened).

